: "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Accurately use information about people's past experiences, interests, hobbies in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Describes events that happened at work, using appropriate expressions and well-constructed simple past phrases."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "  Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Describes events that happened at work, using appropriate expressions and well-constructed simple past phrases."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Describes events that happened at work, using appropriate expressions and well-constructed simple past phrases."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Describes events that happened at work, using appropriate expressions and well-constructed simple past phrases."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Opening a Meeting"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The Chairperson usually opens a meeting. To \u2018open a meeting' means to <span class=\"italic\">start a meeting</span>.<br /><br /> You use the Simple Present to open meetings. A meeting can start with a roundtable. A \u2018roundtable' is when you go around the table and each person introduces themselves.<br /><br />  Then, the Chairperson reads the items (a list of things to be discussed) on the agenda. You use verbs with Infinitives like <span class=\"italic\">need to</span> or <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> to talk about the items of the meeting. The agenda is the list of things to talk about. You talk about each item separately.<br /><br />  The Chairperson usually asks for additions to the agenda -- meaning other things you want to talk about during the meeting."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'd like to start with a roundtable. Please introduce yourself.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The points on the agenda today are \u2026"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Are there any additions to the agenda?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We need to talk about the following items in the agenda."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "boardroom "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " the place where you have meetings "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This is a large boardroom."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear in a meeting."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "chairperson "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the person who runs a meeting "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Who is the chairperson of today's meeting?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "agenda  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the items to discuss in a meeting "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are four points on the agenda today."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "objectives "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a goal; something you hope to get "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Our objective is to sell 500 products per month."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to participate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to talk and ask questions in a meeting. "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm happy to participate in the meeting today."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "participation "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "being active; talking and asking questions (in a meeting) "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Thank you for your excellent participation in the meeting."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to get started "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to begin "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Everyone is here.  Let's get started."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "short notice "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "you were not told about something a long time before "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm sorry for the short notice about today's meeting."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob01aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "roundtable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a time in a meeting where each person says something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I'd like to start with a roundtable. Please introduce yourself."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob01aud09"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn3le07ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think about questions or problems you have with your neighbors."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write your agenda for the meeting."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include 4 - 6 items."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Show your agenda to a partner. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss the items."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I think of questions and problems for a meeting."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write an agenda for a meeting."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss possible solutions to problems."}]}], "type": "sena"}